# Role A — Voiceprint tool. Copy to .env.local to override defaults.

# --- Capture store (Role B handoff) — see HANDOFF-A-to-B.md ---
# Persistence is tried in order: Vercel KV → Supabase → forward URL → local file.
#
# 0) Vercel KV / Upstash Redis (deployed default): add the "Upstash for Redis"
#    (KV) integration to the Vercel project and connect it — these two vars are
#    injected automatically, no copy/paste. Submissions then persist + show in
#    /champions with a "live capture" chip.
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
#
# 1) Supabase: B creates the `leads` table, gives you these.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_LEADS_TABLE=leads        # override if B uses a different table name
#
# 2) Or forward to a B-owned endpoint that inserts the row:
# LEAD_FORWARD_URL=
# LEAD_FORWARD_KEY=

# --- Claude prompts (Role D) — see D-DELIVERABLES.md ---
# With this set, /api/voiceprint uses D's Claude voiceprint prompt (model
# claude-opus-4-8) and /api/score uses the champion-scoring prompt. Without it,
# the voiceprint falls back to the local analyzer and /api/score returns 503.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
